/// M07 CORE-021 "formats documents: 9 assert roots green".
/// Source: tests/integration/formats_test.go symbol
/// TestCurrentFormatsDocuments (L49-156).
/// Related fixture: tests/integration/testdata/formats/main.can (read at
/// L30, staged pristine as src/main.can at L46).
/// Disposition: RETAIN (migrate row; the old Go harness stays until the
/// integrator retires it after every linked row, variant, environment and
/// control has accepted evidence).
/// Protects (this file): canlc assert green with a passed report carrying
/// exactly 9 roots: emit 1, toml_port 1, yaml_n 1, json5_n 1, tally 1,
/// jsonl_count 1, main 3 (Go assert leg L70-73; counts grounded per
/// function in main.can).
/// Live document semantics (exact outputs, 64-bit numbers, blank lines,
/// usage, missing-file and malformed-input errors) live in
/// core-021-formats-semantics.can; the ok/fault production process shape
/// lives in core-021-run-shape.can.
/// Variants: none in this file (default only); the usage, valid-document
/// and fault variants belong to the sibling files.
/// Environment: CAN_BUN_ARCHIVE + macOS sandbox-exec; requires
/// can-bun-archive, macos-sandbox-exec. Logical gates SUITE/DIAG/FAULT and
/// C/R/N/S/A identities bind at P23; no live run now. Descriptor timeout
/// 360000ms mirrors the Go 6-minute ctx (L55).
/// Delegated oracles: none.
/// Execution credit: NOT claimed (accept_after P23 unmet).
/// Case formats/documents-roots checks: assert-green, report-passed,
/// root-count, fixture-name, emit-roots, toml-roots, yaml-roots,
/// json5-roots, tally-roots, jsonl-roots, main-roots.
/// Facet map (formats_test.go legs): assert-green pins the assert leg
/// (L70-73: status 0 and empty diagnostics or the test fatals);
/// report-passed pins the implied report leg (exit 0 with empty
/// diagnostics means the assert report passes; the Go test returns here
/// without parsing the report JSON, so the passed flag is recorded from
/// the green status, not a parsed field); root-count pins the nine roots
/// (counted verbatim from the fixture asserts rows below; the Go test
/// pins no count, so 9 = 1+1+1+1+1+1+3 is fixture-derived);
/// fixture-name grounds the pins in the staged fixture (L30: main.can;
/// L46: src/main.can); emit-roots pins emit (fixture L18-19: sample "hi"
/// => ok 2, 1 root); toml-roots pins toml_port (fixture L34-35: sample
/// "svc.toml" => ok 8080, 1 root); yaml-roots pins yaml_n (fixture
/// L54-55: sample "point.yaml" => ok 7, 1 root); json5-roots pins
/// json5_n (fixture L74-75: sample "point.json5" => ok 7, 1 root);
/// tally-roots pins tally (fixture L94-95: sample waypoint("a", 1) => ok,
/// 1 root); jsonl-roots pins jsonl_count (fixture L101-102: sample
/// "points.jsonl" => ok 2, 1 root); main-roots pins main (fixture
/// L127-130: empty/badop/arity => ok, 3 roots; the when-sample clauses
/// at fixture L23-27/L39-40/L59-60/L79-80/L104-105/L113-114/L119-120 are
/// fixtures, not roots).
/// Shared old files untouched; retirement is a later integrator decision.
